# Issue-driven development (identity-service)

When the user asks to implement work, assume it maps to a GitHub Issue unless they say otherwise.

## Before coding

1. Identify the issue: `gh issue view <n> -R SydLabs9/identity-service`
2. Confirm labels (`auth`, `authz`, `infrastructure`, `documentation`) and milestone (e.g. v0.4.0).
3. Branch from `dev`: `feature/<issue-n>-<short-name>` or `fix/<issue-n>-<short-name>`
   - PR target: **`SydLabs9/identity-service:dev`** (from personal fork if applicable)

## While working

- Reference the issue in commit messages: `feat(auth): JWT issuer (#15)`
- Update `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` for user-visible changes.
- Do not close issues until tests pass and the user agrees the scope is done.

## After merge-ready work

1. Open PR to `dev` (template reminds CHANGELOG + tests).
2. Comment on the issue with what shipped and link the PR:
   `gh issue comment <n> -R SydLabs9/identity-service --body "..."`
3. Close only when acceptance criteria are met:
   `gh issue close <n> -R SydLabs9/identity-service`
4. For release milestones: move `[Unreleased]` → version section in CHANGELOG, merge `dev` → `main`, tag, `gh release create`.

## Roadmap and project board

- Keep [docs/ROADMAP.md](docs/ROADMAP.md) and [product/SCOPE.md](product/SCOPE.md) in sync when priorities or issue numbers change.
- Org board: https://github.com/orgs/SydLabs9/projects/1/views/1 — remind user to move cards (Done / In Progress) if CLI lacks `project` scope.
- To add issues via CLI: `gh auth refresh -s read:project,project` then `gh project item-add 1 --owner SydLabs9 --url <issue-url>`

## Scope guardrails (generic auth/authz service)

- **Authentication** (credentials, tokens, JWKS) before **authorization** (roles, clients, policies).
- Do not implement OAuth2/OIDC gateway (#21) before JWT baseline (#15–#18) unless the user explicitly reprioritizes.
- Prefer incremental releases (SemVer) over large unreviewable diffs.

## Useful commands

```bash
gh issue list -R SydLabs9/identity-service --state open
gh issue list -R SydLabs9/identity-service --label auth --state open
gh issue view 15 -R SydLabs9/identity-service
gh pr create --base dev --head feature/15-jwt --title "feat(auth): JWT access tokens (#15)"
```
